            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EThis week Sebastiaan and Lotte take a look at two community packages that landed recently on the Umbraco marketplace, both adding the ability to allow editors to manage tabular data for properties: Webwonders \u200BUmbraco \u200BTable\u200BEditor and Umb\u200BHost \u200BTables.\n\n\u0026#128230; Webwonders \u200BUmbraco \u200BTable\u200BEditor on the Umbraco Marketplace: https://marketplace.umbraco.com/package/webwonders.umbraco.tableeditor\n\u0026#128230; Umb\u200BHost \u200BTables on the Umbraco Marketplace: https://marketplace.umbraco.com/package/umbhost.tables\n\n--------\n\u2753 Looking for help with your Umbraco projects? Visit the Forum\n https://forum.umbraco.com\n \n\u0026#128172; Want to chat with the friendly Umbraco Community? Join our Discord server\n https://discord.umbraco.com\n \n\u2709\uFE0F Got a question (or topic suggestion) for the HQ Developer Relations team?\n https://umbra.co/contact-devrel, or the \u2018contact-devrel\u2019 channel on Discord\n \n#Umbraco\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CuBm41uczBM\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noopener\u0022\u003ERead the original article\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
